WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.534
-Welcome back, Jon.
-Ahh!

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.133
-You know,
it is your 10th appearance.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:08.067
-Double dige!
-Double digits!

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:11.000
-Double dige!
-I'm so happy!

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.734
Double dige! I'm so happy.
-Aww.

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.400
-10th appearance.
-That means you like me.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.267
-I love you.
I more than like you.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:19.200
Please, come on
for another 50 appearances.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.934
-Oh, okay.
-A thousand appearances.

00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:23.300
-You have to give me
my beard back.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:27.267
-Yeah, I kind of am
trying to figure this out.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.467
I'm not sure where it is.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.067
-It looks fantastic.
-Really?

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.133
-I'm on board. I'm on --

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:32.667
[ Applause ]

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:36.934
The people have spoken.

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:39.300
-I want to thank you also
for helping me out.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.067
You did an episode of
"Password."

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:42.868
-How much fun did we have?
-We had the best time

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.300
in "Password,"
and thank you for doing that.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.701
You came on, and it was

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:48.334
a tribute to Betty White,
that show.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:50.634
-The best.
-It was our first show.

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.133
You did me a solid.
Thank you for that.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:53.868
Remember, we did a sketch
with Betty White?

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:55.267
-Oh, my God.
-For the Emmys?

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:59.267
-It was a "Glee" parody.
-Yes.

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:00.434
-6B.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:03.767
-It was
"Studio 6B, a 'Glee' Parody."

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:09.133
-And my job was to
back that thang up.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.334
-Yeah.

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:13.367
Into Betty White's...front.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:15.000
[ Cheering ]

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.267
-She was like a choreographer.

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:19.234
She was like, "Back that
thing up, back that..."

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:21.033
How funny was Betty White?
-She was in her 90s.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:23.334
-The greatest.
-God bless her.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.033
-God bless Betty White.
She was the greatest.

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:27.434
-My favorite part was,
the continuation of that was

00:01:27.434 --> 00:01:28.901
that we had kind of
a quick change after that,

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:32.534
and I had to present
right after that with Betty,

00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:35.300
And it was awesome, but I had to
get out of my "Glee" costume,

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.200
and into my tuxedo.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.734
So I had to do like,
a quick change backstage,

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:40.968
and Betty was right there.

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:43.367
-In front of Betty?
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:45.801
-And by the way,
did not look away.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.334
-Wow!

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:50.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.200
Betty White is a legend.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.834
I love that.
-Took it in. She took it in.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:01.534
-I haven't seen you
since you owned the summer

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:04.234
with the blockbuster,
"Top Gun: Maverick."

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.734
No big deal.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:06.934
[ Applause ]

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.901
The biggest movie ever made.
Come on, buddy!

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:13.801
-I can't wait till they
re-release it 15 years later,

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:17.100
"Avatar" style.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.133
-Dude, I saw you on
the on the big screen,

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.167
but I saw you
on the biggest screen.

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:22.834
Oh, the IMAX? Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:24.434
I loved it.
-It's kind of an experience.

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:26.567
-Dude, your movie was
the greatest thing.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.934
-Did that spontaneously
make you grow that beard?

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:30.868
Watching that, it was just so
testosterone-filled?

00:02:30.868 --> 00:02:32.467
-So action-packed, like...

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.501
And then, you know,
I saw the movie,

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:39.767
and then I go, and I went
to a great restaurant.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:40.767
Emilio's Ballato.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.267
-I forgot about this.

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:44.534
-And this is
an Italian restaurant,

00:02:44.534 --> 00:02:46.734
opening weekend
of "Top Gun: Maverick,"

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:49.868
and I happen to run into there,
my best bud, Jon Hamm.

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:51.767
-Yes.
-Was there eating dinner

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.534
at this restaurant.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:55.334
-You were two-timing me, though.

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:57.767
You were there with Harry Kane.

00:02:57.767 --> 00:02:59.234
-I was there with Harry Kane.

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:01.033
-Talking football, I'm assuming.
-Yeah.

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:02.367
-[In British accent] Football.

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:04.234
-[In British accent]
Yeah, we were talkin' football.

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:06.868
-Let's get some Italian food.

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:08.367
-It's what people like.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:11.334
You go and you play football,
you get Italian food.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:13.868
-Some pasta.
-Pasta.

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:16.567
-Maybe some, like,
eggplant parm.

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.934
-Your ravioli.
-Whatever. Whatever.

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.801
-Whatever.
-Don't even matter.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:23.200
-Doesn't matter, does it?
-Don't even matter.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.100
-Does it?
-Just buds.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.434
-Does it? Spuds.
-Buds and spuds.

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:29.634
-Oh, buds and spuds.
Exactly right.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:30.901
[In normal voice]
So I was there cheating on you.

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.634
Yeah, with Harry.

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:34.400
Thank God we weren't
sitting together.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.067
We would have done this
all night.

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:37.400
-The whole restaurant
would have left.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.200
-No, but I was happy to see you,
because it was a big --

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.934
-Yeah, yeah.
You gave me a nice gift.

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:42.501
That was really sweet of you.
-Do you remember?

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:44.367
-I do, the waiter came over

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:47.701
with a sort of dirty plate
and half a meatball on it

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:50.868
and said, "Mr. Fallon would
like to gift this to you."

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.801
-Yeah, I gave you
half of meatball.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.467
-And I ate it.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:56.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:59.534
-Good meatball.

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:01.534
[British accent] Good meatball.
-[British accent] Meatball.

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:02.667
-Great meatball, mate.
-Play football

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:04.634
and great meatball.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:06.901
Football, meatball.
-Football, meatball.

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:09.868
Half a meatball. Meat-foot.
-Meat-foot..

00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:11.133
We...

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:12.300
You know what it is?
I saw you there, and I go,

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.901
oh, I don't know
if you recognize me,

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:15.834
so I want to to send him over
something

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:17.834
to congratulate him,
because "Top Gun" was already...

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:19.734
-You weren't in disguise.

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:22.868
-I didn't have a beard then.
-You did not have a beard then.

00:04:22.868 --> 00:04:24.300
-But yeah, I guess it is was
a small restaurant.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.367
I guess you did see me,
but didn't want to bother you.

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:29.000
But I thought it'd be funny
to send you over something.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.767
I go, I'll send over a meatball.
That'll make him laugh.

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:33.501
Then I go, no, no, no.
[British accent] Wait, wait.

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:34.467
-[British accent] Wait.
-Wait, come back here.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.601
-Oy.
-Oy! Oy.

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:38.300
Back here.
-Oy, waiter!

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.033
-Hey.
-Oy, an old meatball.

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:42.467
-Oh, now, -- now --

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:45.868
[Accent becomes gravely]
No, now I'm turning to Statham.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.467
-[Imitating Jason Statham]
Are you gonna be Jason Statham?

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:48.534
-Jason Statham?

00:04:48.534 --> 00:04:51.968
Give him half a meatball.
-Half a meatball.

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:53.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.667
-Give him the ol' demi-ball.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:57.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.434
-Give him the 180.

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:01.734
[In normal voice]
You've already starred in

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.300
one of the greatest TV
shows of all time.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.734
-Thank you.
-"Mad Men."

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:05.901
-Oh, that one.
-Yeah.

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:07.467
[ Applause ]
A little hit.

00:05:07.467 --> 00:05:09.367
-Pretty good. Pretty good.

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:11.334
Yeah, kind of a home run.
-Had a good run.

00:05:11.334 --> 00:05:13.100
Had a good run. A good run.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:16.601
-But now you're returning to TV
with not one, but two shows.

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:19.167
-Double dip.
-Wow. Double digits, double dip.

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:21.300
-Double dige, double dip.
-Yeah "Fargo."

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:25.100
-Half a meatball, two meatball.
Double dip, who cares?

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.701
-"Fargo."

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:28.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:30.501
"Fargo" and "The Morning Show."

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:31.567
-"Fargo."

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.234
-I like going off
the rails with you.

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:34.300
It's fun. Why not?

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.634
Wait, "Fargo."

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.200
-"Fargo," it's a fantastic show.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.234
Each season sort of reimagines
the whole story,

00:05:40.234 --> 00:05:41.534
although they are kind of --

00:05:41.534 --> 00:05:43.000
Rock was on it last year.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.634
It was in Kansas City
in the '30s.

00:05:44.634 --> 00:05:47.033
-Chris Rock was on "Fargo."
-Yes, it was great.

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:48.567
It was great
to see him doing all that.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:50.000
-That's gonna be
a great fit for you.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.934
-So this one does not take place
in Kansas City in the '30s,

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:54.868
but it does sort of,
keeps imagining organized crime

00:05:54.868 --> 00:05:55.934
and what's happening.

00:05:55.934 --> 00:05:58.567
I play a rather
unsavory character.

00:05:58.567 --> 00:06:00.167
-Ooh.
-I can't really get into it.

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:02.767
-Wow. You can't get into it?

00:06:02.767 --> 00:06:05.000
-Well, I mean,
I'm gonna very into it.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.634
I can't give deets.

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:10.567
And "The Morning Show."
I get to hang out with Aniston.

00:06:10.567 --> 00:06:12.234
-Reese Witherspoon.
-Reese.

00:06:12.234 --> 00:06:13.734
-Billy Crudup.
-Billy Cruds.

00:06:13.734 --> 00:06:15.100
-Oh, I love that dude.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.868
-Great cast, great people.

00:06:17.868 --> 00:06:19.501
I can't really get into it.

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:21.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.267 --> 00:06:22.400
-"I can't get into it
right now."

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.467
-I'd love to get it.
I just can't.

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:27.334
Oh, I can't get into it.
-"I just can't talk."

00:06:27.334 --> 00:06:29.133
Well, I want to talk about this
film, "Confess, Fletch."

00:06:29.133 --> 00:06:30.734
-You know I'm a giant
"Fletch" fan.

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:33.367
We've talked about this,
but this is a great story.

00:06:33.367 --> 00:06:34.901
-We did it. We actually made it.

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:38.634
It's in theaters and on
digital platforms near you.

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:40.100
-"Confess, Fletch."

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.701
-It's the second book
in the series.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:43.801
When they made that movie
with Chevy Chase,

00:06:43.801 --> 00:06:48.267
very famously inaugurated
that film franchise

00:06:48.267 --> 00:06:50.534
and put his stamp right on it.

00:06:50.534 --> 00:06:52.334
So we were like, "Oh, God.

00:06:52.334 --> 00:06:54.400
I don't want to do
a Chevy impression."

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:55.667
-Yeah, of course.

00:06:55.667 --> 00:06:57.000
-And I don't want to, you know,
steal his bits.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.667
So we went back to the books,
and there's 11 novels

00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:01.267
that Gregory McDonald
wrote over the course

00:07:01.267 --> 00:07:02.467
of the '70s and '80s,

00:07:02.467 --> 00:07:04.334
and they're really funny
and they're fun.

00:07:04.334 --> 00:07:06.834
And we just kind of took it
back to the page.

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:08.934
-But you watched "Fletch"
when it first came out with --

00:07:08.934 --> 00:07:10.000
-Oh, my God, did I ever?

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.501
I saw it at
the Wehrenberg Theater

00:07:11.501 --> 00:07:12.934
in Saint Louis, Missouri.

00:07:12.934 --> 00:07:15.734
[ Applause ]

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:17.234
I thought maybe there was
some Wehrenbergs in town.

00:07:17.234 --> 00:07:18.634
-Why would that get applause?

00:07:18.634 --> 00:07:20.801
We're not in Saint Louis.

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:23.801
-Right? Everybody gets it.

00:07:23.801 --> 00:07:26.334
-You saw it in Times Square
in New York City.

00:07:26.334 --> 00:07:28.000
[ Applause ]

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.267
You'll never forget it.
-Never forget it.

00:07:30.267 --> 00:07:32.334
-Never forget going to Times
Square and watching "Fletch."

00:07:32.334 --> 00:07:34.000
-When I was 14, somehow.
-Yeah.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.100
-Wildly dangerous,
in the '80s, by myself.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.400
-Yeah, well, you saw it
and you loved it.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:40.734
-I saw it and loved it.

00:07:40.734 --> 00:07:42.634
-But you got into it and you go,
"I'm going to watch this.

00:07:42.634 --> 00:07:44.133
I'm obsessed with this movie."

00:07:44.133 --> 00:07:46.400
And then you realized that it
was based on based on a book.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.467
And so I was like,
"Wait, there's more?

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:48.767
There's more stories?"

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:50.300
And I immediately went
to the bookstore

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.300
and realized I had no money,

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.501
so I stole all of the paperbacks
that I could steal.

00:07:54.501 --> 00:07:56.234
-How did you steal
11 paperbacks?

00:07:56.234 --> 00:07:58.901
-Not at once!
-Oh, alright.

00:07:58.901 --> 00:08:02.000
You went back and stole more?
-One at a time.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.767
-Wow.
-Then they don't see.

00:08:03.767 --> 00:08:04.968
They don't think
they're missing.

00:08:04.968 --> 00:08:06.000
-Do the people
at Walden Books --

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.434
-If you take
the whole section out,

00:08:07.434 --> 00:08:08.934
the guy's like,
"What are you doing?"

00:08:08.934 --> 00:08:12.367
You take one, it's like,
"Hey, what is that over there?

00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:14.133
That's weird. Oh, yeah."

00:08:14.133 --> 00:08:16.667
-So you stole all
of the "Fletch" books?

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:18.167
-I sure did.

00:08:18.167 --> 00:08:21.567
And now I'm gonna steal
the franchise from Chevy.

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:23.167
-Yeah, exactly.
But here you are.

00:08:23.167 --> 00:08:27.634
Will you make all 11 movies?
-I hope.

00:08:27.634 --> 00:08:30.100
That's up to America
to decide, but...

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:32.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:32.701 --> 00:08:34.567
And all the foreign territories.

00:08:34.567 --> 00:08:37.334
But I really hope to.

00:08:37.334 --> 00:08:39.501
Obviously, it's set up to be,
you know,

00:08:39.501 --> 00:08:41.133
kind of a franchise
in the making.

00:08:41.133 --> 00:08:42.634
-How do we describe
"Confess, Fletch"?

00:08:42.634 --> 00:08:45.467
-It's a whodunit,
and by the end,

00:08:45.467 --> 00:08:49.467
you definitely find out
who done it.

00:08:49.467 --> 00:08:51.467
I mean, that delivers
right there on its promise.

00:08:51.467 --> 00:08:52.501
-It delivers?
-Yeah.

00:08:52.501 --> 00:08:53.868
-But it's a funny, you know...

00:08:53.868 --> 00:08:55.934
He talks his way out of trouble

00:08:55.934 --> 00:08:58.367
that he's already
talked himself into,

00:08:58.367 --> 00:08:59.934
so that's kind of
perfect for me.

00:08:59.934 --> 00:09:01.300
-Yeah, it's actually great.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:03.067
I can't think of a better person
to play Fletch.

00:09:03.067 --> 00:09:04.167
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:09:04.167 --> 00:09:06.367
Here is Jon Hamm in
"Confess, Fletch."

00:09:06.367 --> 00:09:07.667
Take a look.

00:09:07.667 --> 00:09:09.834
-So what do we know
about this victim?

00:09:09.834 --> 00:09:11.133
-Like we're going to tell you.

00:09:11.133 --> 00:09:13.300
-Laurel Goodwin's from Westover,
was living in Allstrom

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:17.200
with two roommates, worked at
a Cambridge cafe as a barista.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.601
-We're telling you.

00:09:18.601 --> 00:09:23.467
-Ms. Goodwin was pursuing
a career in the art world.

00:09:23.467 --> 00:09:24.801
-Hmm.
-Interesting connection.

00:09:24.801 --> 00:09:28.267
-Well, I've either just
walked into a frame-up,

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:31.667
or somebody from my past
is trying to get revenge on me.

00:09:31.667 --> 00:09:33.200
-Who hates you?

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.200
Besides Griz.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.467
-Well, I did put quite a few
prominent people away

00:09:37.467 --> 00:09:40.000
when I was
a very famous reporter

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.701
at the "News Tribune"
in Los Angeles.

00:09:41.701 --> 00:09:43.601
-I looked into
your criminal record.

00:09:43.601 --> 00:09:44.634
-And?

00:09:44.634 --> 00:09:46.701
-Bad check charge.
-Eh.

00:09:46.701 --> 00:09:48.367
-Two contempt of court charges.
-Pfft.

00:09:48.367 --> 00:09:51.868
-A number of nonpayment
of alimony charges.

00:09:51.868 --> 00:09:56.300
-100% of most of
those were dismissed.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:58.767
-You're a bit of
a shady character, Mr. Fletcher.

00:09:58.767 --> 00:10:00.868
-But I am adorable.

00:10:00.868 --> 00:10:03.133
-Yeah! That's right.

00:10:03.133 --> 00:10:05.300
Jon Hamm, everybody!
-Heyo!

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:06.601
-"Confess, Fletch."

00:10:06.601 --> 00:10:08.367
When we come back, Jon and I
are going head-to-head

00:10:08.367 --> 00:10:09.467
in the game of "Hey, Robot."

00:10:09.467 --> 00:10:10.467
-Hey, Robot!
-Stick around.

